# A Low-Tech, Hands-On Approach To Teaching Sorting Algorithms to Working Students.

**Authors:** Dios, R., Geller, J.

## Abstract
Focuses on identifying the educational effects of "activity oriented" instructional techniques. Examines which instructional methods produce enhanced learning and comprehension. Discusses the problem of learning "sorting algorithms," a major topic in every Computer Science curriculum. Presents a low-tech, hands-on teaching method for sorting algorithms. (Author/AEF)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ577855

